"Coarse salt and freshly ground pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "coarse salt and freshly ground pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Peel, core and slice the pears. Simmer them in water for 10 minutes, then add the beans. Cook them until almost done but still a vivid green."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Meanwhile, fry the bacon until crisp. Remove from pan and drain on paper towels. Add the vegetables, toss in the fat and add the remaining ingredients. Cover and simmer until the beans are cooked."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Crumble the bacon over the pears and beans and serve."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 409.4, "protein_g": 9.7, "carbohydrates_g": 62.1, "fat_g": 17.0, "saturated_fat_g": 5.7, "trans_fat_g": 0.1, "cholesterol_mg": 28.7, "sodium_mg": 1197.3, "fiber_g": 14.3, "sugar_g": 38.3, "unsaturated_fat_g": 10.1, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["german"], "diet": [], "course": ["side dish"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["bacon", "boil", "easy", "fall", "fry", "green bean", "pear", "quick", "vegetables"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 9}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1982-10-31", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T01:38:21.447541+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "biscotti", "nyt_id": 10766, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/10766-biscotti", "name": "Biscotti", "author": "Molly O’Neill", "description": "These classic Italian cookies get their signature crispness from being twice-baked: First, the dough is cooked in logs, cut into slices, then baked again. Because they travel and keep well, a pile of them makes an excellent gift wrapped in a cellophane bag and tied with a ribbon. Feel free to experiment with add-ins: Sub in hazelnuts or pistachios for the almonds. Add mini chocolate chips or dried cranberries, or a teaspoon of citrus zest. Or take the cookies over the top by drizzling with melted chocolate, glazing with icing or dusting with sprinkles. You do you.", "servings": {"text": "About 24 cookies", "min": 24, "max": 24, "yield_type": "pieces"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 60, "raw": {"total": "1 hour"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 vanilla bean, split in half lengthwise", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "vanilla bean", "preparation": "split in half lengthwise", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "¾ cup granulated sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 0.75, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "granulated sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "½ cup unsalted butter, at room temperature", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "unsalted butter", "preparation": "at room temperature", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 eggs", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "eggs", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "2 teaspoons vanilla extract", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "vanilla extract", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "2 cups all-purpose flour", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "all-purpose flour", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 ½ teaspoons baking powder", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "baking powder", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "½ teaspoon fine sea salt", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "fine sea salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 ¼ cups slivered almonds, coarsely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "slivered almonds", "preparation": "coarsely chopped", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Heat the oven to 325 degrees. Position rack in center of oven. With a small knife, scrape the seeds from the vanilla bean and place in a small bowl. Add the sugar and use your fingers to mix the vanilla evenly into the sugar. Set aside. With an electric mixer, cream the butter until light. Add the vanilla sugar and mix until fluffy. Add the eggs and the vanilla extract and mix until smooth. Stir together the flour, baking powder, salt and almonds and stir into the butter mixture."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Line a baking sheet with parchment paper. Divide the dough into 3 pieces. On a lightly floured surface, shape each piece of dough into a log that is about 1 ¼ inches in diameter. Place the logs on the baking sheet, spacing them as far apart as possible. Bake in the center of the oven until lightly browned, about 30 minutes."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Place the logs on a cutting board and let them cool slightly. With a serrated knife, cut the logs on the diagonal into ½-inch-thick pieces. Place on the baking sheet, cut side down. Bake until lightly browned, about 15 minutes, turning once. Transfer the cookies to a rack to cool. Store in an airtight container."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 135.5, "protein_g": 2.8, "carbohydrates_g": 15.6, "fat_g": 7.1, "saturated_fat_g": 2.7, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 23.5, "sodium_mg": 73.1, "fiber_g": 1.0, "sugar_g": 6.6, "unsaturated_fat_g": 4.0, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["italian"], "diet": [], "course": ["dessert"], "meal": ["snack"], "occasion": ["christmas"], "other": ["almond", "bake", "christmas cookie", "cookie", "make-ahead", "vanilla bean", "baking"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2019/11/26/dining/vanilla-biscotti/vanilla-biscotti-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 2024}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1993-05-23", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T01:48:41.317789+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "bitter-green-pesto", "nyt_id": 10882, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/10882-bitter-green-pesto", "name": "Bitter Green Pesto", "author": "Molly O’Neill", "description": "This variation of the traditional pesto is sharp and should be used moderately on fish, chicken, pasta or steamed new potatoes, but because it is rather bitter, should not be used as a marinade. Bitter green pesto also adds zest when used as a garnish on gazpacho, cold tomato soup or other cold vegetable soups.", "servings": {"text": "One and one-quarter cups", "min": 1, "max": 1, "yield_type": "volume"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 10, "raw": {"total": "10 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "2 cups stemmed arugula", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "stemmed arugula", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "2 cups stemmed watercress", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "stemmed watercress", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "6 scallions, green part only, coarsely chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "scallions", "preparation": "green part only, coarsely chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "8 cloves roasted garlic, peeled", "group": null, "quantity": 8.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "clove", "item": "roasted garlic", "preparation": "peeled", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 teaspoon salt", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "⅛ teaspoon freshly ground black pepper", "group": null, "quantity": 0.125, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "freshly ground black pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "½ cup olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Place the arugula, watercress, scallions, roasted garlic, salt and pepper in a food processor and process until finely chopped. With the machine running, slowly pour in the olive oil. Process until smooth, stopping to scrape sides of the bowl. Store in an airtight container."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 414.1, "protein_g": 2.3, "carbohydrates_g": 6.6, "fat_g": 43.4, "saturated_fat_g": 6.0, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 0.0, "sodium_mg": 301.0, "fiber_g": 1.5, "sugar_g": 1.3, "unsaturated_fat_g": 36.2, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": [], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["arugula", "condiments", "dips and spreads", "scallion", "watercress"]}, "images": [], "rating": null, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1993-08-01", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T01:53:39.612796+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "bitter-greens-with-sour-cream-dressing", "nyt_id": 10682, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/10682-bitter-greens-with-sour-cream-dressing", "name": "Bitter Greens With Sour-Cream Dressing", "author": "Mark Bittman", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 15, "raw": {"total": "15 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "3 hard-cooked eggs", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "hard-cooked eggs", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 teaspoon sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tsp", "item": "sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "Juice of 1 lemon, or to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "juice of 1 lemon", "preparation": "or to taste", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 cup sour cream", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "sour cream", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 tablespoon milk", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "milk", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "Salt and pepper to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt and pepper to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "6 cups greens, preferably romaine, endive, escarole, radicchio or chicory, roughly chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "greens", "preparation": "preferably romaine, endive, escarole, radicchio or chicory, roughly chopped", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Cut eggs in two and put yolks in a bowl. Mash yolks with sugar and lemon juice, and beat in the sour cream with a wooden spoon, until smooth. Thin with milk if necessary. Season with salt and pepper. (This can all be done in a food processor or a mixer, but it is easy enough by hand.)"}, {"position": 2, "text": "Slice egg whites into thin strips, and toss with greens and dressing. Serve."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 186.2, "protein_g": 6.5, "carbohydrates_g": 8.9, "fat_g": 14.7, "saturated_fat_g": 6.9, "trans_fat_g": 0.5, "cholesterol_mg": 146.2, "sodium_mg": 428.7, "fiber_g": 2.2, "sugar_g": 4.9, "unsaturated_fat_g": 4.9, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": ["gluten-free"], "course": ["side dish"], "meal": [], "occasion": ["mother’s day"], "other": ["bitter greens", "easy", "egg", "green salad", "quick", "sour cream", "spring", "weeknight"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 5}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2003-07-02", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T01:44:48.015437+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "bitter-herbs-salad", "nyt_id": 12360, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/12360-bitter-herbs-salad", "name": "Bitter Herbs Salad", "author": "Martha Rose Shulman", "description": "Bitter herbs – the maror – are part of the Seder ritual, symbolizing the bitterness of slavery experienced by the Jews in Egypt. Endive, romaine and chicory (for which I’ve substituted radicchio) are present on many Sephardic ritual platters, but often they also appear in salads served with the meal. This can be served as a separate course or as a side dish.", "servings": {"text": "6 servings", "min": 6, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 15, "raw": {"total": "15 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "2 hearts of romaine lettuce", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "hearts of romaine lettuce", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 small head radicchio", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "small head radicchio", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 Belgian endives", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "belgian endives", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 ½ cups arugula or watercress, washed and dried", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "arugula or watercress", "preparation": "washed and dried", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 rib celery, preferably from the heart, sliced very thin", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "rib celery", "preparation": "preferably from the heart, sliced very thin", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "2 scallions, chopped (optional)", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "scallions", "preparation": "chopped", "optional": true}, {"position": 7, "raw": "¼ cup chopped flat-leaf parsley", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "chopped flat-leaf parsley", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "¼ cup chopped fresh dill", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "chopped fresh dill", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 tablespoon chopped fresh mint (optional)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "chopped fresh mint", "preparation": null, "optional": true}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 small garlic clove", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "small garlic clove", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "Salt to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "3 tablespoons freshly squeezed lemon juice", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "freshly squeezed lemon juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "½ cup extra virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "cup", "item": "extra virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Wash and dry the romaine lettuce leaves and break into medium pieces. Separate the radicchio leaves and cut into medium pieces. Rinse and dry the endives and slice crosswise about ¾ inch thick. Toss together all of the greens, the celery and the scallions in a large salad bowl and sprinkle the herbs over the top."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Skin the garlic clove, cut in half and remove green shoots. Place in a mortar and pestle with a generous pinch of salt and mash to a paste. Work in the lemon juice and then the olive oil. Taste and adjust salt. Transfer to a jar until ready to serve the salad."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Just before serving, shake the dressing in the jar, pour over the salad and toss."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 187.1, "protein_g": 1.8, "carbohydrates_g": 5.8, "fat_g": 18.4, "saturated_fat_g": 2.5, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 0.0, "sodium_mg": 377.0, "fiber_g": 2.9, "sugar_g": 1.6, "unsaturated_fat_g": 15.3, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["mediterranean"], "diet": ["dairy-free", "gluten-free", "healthy", "high fiber", "low-sodium", "vegan", "vegetarian"], "course": [], "meal": [], "occasion": ["passover"], "other": ["dill", "easy", "low cholesterol", "parsley", "quick", "salad", "spring"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2012/04/03/health/nutrition/03recipehealth/03recipehealth-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}], "rating": {"average": 5.0, "count": 230}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2012-04-03", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T23:55:50.588881+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "bittersweet-salad", "nyt_id": 6990, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/6990-bittersweet-salad", "name": "Bittersweet Salad", "author": "Florence Fabricant", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": 15, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 15, "raw": {"total": "15 minutes", "prep": "15 minutes"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 bunch dandelion leaves, baby mustard greens, arugula or watercress", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "bunch", "item": "dandelion leaves", "preparation": "baby mustard greens, arugula or watercress", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 head radicchio", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "head", "item": "radicchio", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 Belgian endives", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "belgian endives", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 tablespoons fresh mint leaves", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "fresh mint leaves", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "3 tablespoons extra-virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "extra-virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "7 tablespoons balsamic vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 7.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "balsamic vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "4 tablespoons shavings of Parmesan cheese", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "quantity_max": null, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "shavings of parmesan cheese", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "Freshly ground black pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "quantity_max": null, "unit": null, "item": "freshly ground black pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Rinse and dry the dandelion, mustard greens, arugula or watercress. Remove and discard all heavy stems. Place the greens in a salad bowl. Pull apart the leaves from the head of radicchio and tear them into bite-size pieces. Add to the salad bowl. Slice the endive horizontally about one-half inch thick and add the slices to the bowl, breaking them up. Add the mint leaves."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Beat oil and vinegar together, pour over salad ingredients and toss."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Divide salad among four plates and scatter cheese over the top of each. Season with pepper and serve."}], "nutrition": {"calories": 170.3, "protein_g": 4.6, "carbohydrates_g": 9.2, "fat_g": 12.7, "saturated_fat_g": 2.8, "trans_fat_g": 0.0, "cholesterol_mg": 6.3, "sodium_mg": 134.8, "fiber_g": 1.9, "sugar_g": 4.5, "unsaturated_fat_g": 9.3, "source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["mediterranean"], "diet": [], "course": [], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["belgian endive", "dandelion greens", "easy", "parmesan", "quick", "radicchio", "salad", "spring", "weeknight"]}, "images": [], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 7}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1990-04-22", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T00:58:06.159196+00:00", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
